<Project>

  <!--
    Vixen — "the files of this repository", as git defines them, for every test that sweeps the
    tree (#1424). Linked rather than referenced, on the same argument as Vixen.Testing.props beside
    it, and its own file for the reason GoldenFile's is: only the sweeps need it.

    ⚠ A sweep that walks the disk and skips a hand-kept list of directory names answers a different
    question from the one it means, and eighteen copies of that list disagreed about `.nuke`,
    `references/` and everything else a working machine accumulates under .gitignore. Use
    `RepositoryFiles.Files(root, "*.cs")` instead of a walk.

    Consumers need a `using Vixen.Testing;`. It names only the BCL, so a tool links it too.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)RepositoryFiles.cs" Link="Testing\RepositoryFiles.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
